      subgraph 22 ["nyx-engine"]
        style 22 fill:#ffffff,stroke:#2e6295,color:#2e6295

        23["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Commands</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: Rust modules]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>The Engine and its catalog:<br />every action by name with<br />JSON arguments, JSON Schema<br />and JSON reply; the<br />dispatcher; the guide cards a<br />host reads on demand. The<br />window and the MCP server use<br />the same entries.</div>"]
        style 23 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        24["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Project</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: Rust modules]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>The saved state: feature<br />list, mesh settings, one<br />ProblemSpec per physics,<br />project materials. The format<br />key is checked at the file<br />boundary.</div>"]
        style 24 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        25["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Geometry operations</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: Rust modules]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Every edit of a geom feature<br />list as a function that does<br />it or says why not, and the<br />descriptors of the geom<br />operations (they live here<br />because geom depends on serde<br />only).</div>"]
        style 25 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        26["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Job runner and queue</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: Rust modules]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Mesh, solve, convergence and<br />file jobs on their own<br />threads with progress and<br />cancel, queued in lanes<br />(priority, owners in turn,<br />stages shared by content),<br />solves in a worker process<br />(killed on cancel, its stage<br />log mirrored, results read<br />back from a file), memory<br />estimates learned from the<br />workers and admission by free<br />memory, solving physics in<br />the order of the one-way<br />couplings, mesh convergence<br />on a scratch engine.</div>"]
        style 26 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        27["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Command lists</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: Rust modules]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>A JSON-lines list of engine<br />commands is parsed, checked<br />against the catalog and its<br />schemas, planned on a scratch<br />engine (what would be meshed<br />and solved, nothing run) and<br />run in order through<br />Engine::call.</div>"]
        style 27 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        28["<div style='font-weight: bold'>API reference</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: Rust modules]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>One Markdown page per engine<br />command and an index,<br />generated from<br />Engine::catalog() (arguments<br />flattened from the schema, an<br />example that passes the<br />check); docs/api is compared<br />with it by a test.</div>"]
        style 28 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        29["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Meshing seam</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: Rust modules]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>MeshRequest to MeshedModel<br />(mesh, names, label<br />resolver); the only caller of<br />the femcore mesher; absorbing<br />layers across the two halves<br />of a project.</div>"]
        style 29 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        30["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Materials</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: Rust modules]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>The material library plus the<br />materials a project carries,<br />resolved at the study<br />wavelength.</div>"]
        style 30 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        31["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Analyses</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: Rust modules]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Runs the analyses of<br />nyx-analysis on the latest<br />result of a physics.</div>"]
        style 31 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        32["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Results files</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: Rust modules]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>HDF5 results (serial or<br />MPI-IO), the XDMF<br />description, and opening a<br />results file as a project<br />with its results.</div>"]
        style 32 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        33["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Store link</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: Rust modules]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Binds the project to a<br />workflow of the workspace,<br />commits versions, records<br />runs (card and metrics made<br />here).</div>"]
        style 33 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
        34["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Registry and facade</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: Rust modules]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>The physics compiled in<br />(cargo features dfs, sms,<br />ems) and the facade that<br />re-exports what a front-end<br />draws with.</div>"]
        style 34 fill:#85bbf0,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000000
      end

      103["<div style='font-weight: bold'>geom</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Rust library]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Lean CSG-over-B-rep geometry<br />kernel: feature lists, named<br />regions and boundaries,<br />selectors, exact projection<br />oracles. Depends on serde and<br />optional rayon only.</div>"]
      style 103 fill:#438dd5,stroke:#2e6295,color:#ffffff
      111[("<div style='font-weight: bold'>Project file</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: File .nyx.json]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Everything saved for one<br />model: geometry, materials,<br />boundary conditions, studies.<br />JSON with a format key.</div>")]
      style 111 fill:#438dd5,stroke:#2e6295,color:#ffffff
      112[("<div style='font-weight: bold'>Results file</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: File .h5 and .xdmf]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Project, mesh and every<br />solution of every solved<br />physics, compressed, exact;<br />with an XDMF description next<br />to it.</div>")]
      style 112 fill:#438dd5,stroke:#2e6295,color:#ffffff
      114[("<div style='font-weight: bold'>Material library</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Files]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>materials/*.toml next to the<br />program: silicon, silica,<br />sapphire, metals, nitrides,<br />niobate and more, with<br />sources.</div>")]
      style 114 fill:#438dd5,stroke:#2e6295,color:#ffffff
      35["<div style='font-weight: bold'>nyx-physics</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Rust library]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>The Physics trait, the<br />problem envelope<br />(ProblemSpec), descriptors,<br />SolveResult, the registry<br />type, validation, JSON<br />Schemas.</div>"]
      style 35 fill:#438dd5,stroke:#2e6295,color:#ffffff
      41["<div style='font-weight: bold'>nyx-dfs</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Rust library]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Diffusion physics: heat and<br />electrostatics. Typed<br />problem, three-stage kernels,<br />descriptors, goldens.</div>"]
      style 41 fill:#2e7d32,stroke:#205723,color:#ffffff
      47["<div style='font-weight: bold'>nyx-sms</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Rust library]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Solid mechanics: static,<br />eigenfrequency, PML, Floquet,<br />low-reflecting boundaries,<br />axisymmetric.</div>"]
      style 47 fill:#2e7d32,stroke:#205723,color:#ffffff
      56["<div style='font-weight: bold'>nyx-ems</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Rust library]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>EM waves: waveguide modes<br />(real and complex),<br />axisymmetric, cavity in 3D.</div>"]
      style 56 fill:#2e7d32,stroke:#205723,color:#ffffff
      64["<div style='font-weight: bold'>nyx-analysis</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Rust library]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Analyses of results: the<br />polarization (Stokes<br />parameters, Poincare sphere,<br />classes, degenerate groups)<br />as a function of a<br />SolveResult and its mesh.</div>"]
      style 64 fill:#438dd5,stroke:#2e6295,color:#ffffff
      69["<div style='font-weight: bold'>nyx-store</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Rust library]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Workspace, workflow,<br />experiment and run storage:<br />manifests, append-only run<br />log, versions, search, .nyx<br />archives. Knows nothing of a<br />project.</div>"]
      style 69 fill:#438dd5,stroke:#2e6295,color:#ffffff
      78["<div style='font-weight: bold'>femcore</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Rust library]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>The FEM core: meshes, meshing<br />and adaptation, linear<br />algebra behind one driver,<br />finite-element basics, the<br />material specification and<br />library, expressions.</div>"]
      style 78 fill:#438dd5,stroke:#2e6295,color:#ffffff
    end

